&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Join us to help transform how companies around the world run revenue — and build the platform that will guide leading revenue teams into the future&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;At Salesloft, our &lt;strong&gt;Senior Corporate Accountant&lt;/strong&gt; will be pivotal to our company’s success. You will be a key member of our fast-growing and high-performing accounting team. In this role, you will play a crucial part in ensuring the smooth and accurate operation of our &amp;nbsp;&lt;strong&gt;corporate accounting and payroll functions&lt;/strong&gt; &amp;nbsp;across multiple countries, including the US, Mexico, the UK, Poland, India, and other potential markets. This is an excellent opportunity to contribute to a dynamic and fast-paced environment while further developing your skills in US GAAP accounting, international accounting, &lt;strong&gt;US and international payroll processing, tax compliance, and financial reporting.&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;As a &lt;strong&gt;Senior Corporate Accountant&lt;/strong&gt;, you&#39;ll be responsible for &amp;nbsp;&lt;strong&gt;various aspects of corporate accounting and end-to-end payroll administration&lt;/strong&gt;, including &lt;strong&gt;US multi-state payroll, international payroll coordination, tax compliance, financial reporting, and general ledger activities.&lt;/strong&gt;You will play a crucial role in ensuring the accuracy and integrity of our financial records. This includes &lt;strong&gt;processing domestic and global payroll cycles, preparing financial reports, overseeing specific accounting processes such as accounts payable, fixed assets, and accruals, and providing guidance to other team members.&lt;/strong&gt; &amp;nbsp;You will also be involved in &lt;strong&gt;liaising with external auditors, payroll vendors, and supporting internal controls.&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;In addition to working with amazing colleagues who exemplify our ‘team over self’ core value, you will also have the opportunity to be a strategic contributor to our public-readiness journey in a fast-paced goal-oriented accounting and finance department. You will have an opportunity to make a difference.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;WHAT WE’RE LOOKING FOR:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We are seeking a detail-oriented, extremely thorough, and very diligent&lt;strong&gt; Senior Corporate Accountant&lt;/strong&gt; who enjoys working in a fast-paced, high-growth environment.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;If you’re looking for an opportunity to learn more, do more, and become more within &lt;strong&gt;corporate accounting&lt;/strong&gt;, then this is the career path for you!&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;THE TEAM:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Our Salesloft’s Accounting &amp;amp; Finance team is comprised of seasoned and up-and-coming accounting and finance professionals.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The Accounting and Finance team consists of results-oriented SaaS accounting professionals with strong analytical skills ensuring timely and accurate records in accordance with company accounting policies and generally accepted accounting principles. The accountants on our team share a few common traits: they are self-motivated, ambitious, and passionate about redefining the Revenue Orchestration space and activating the authentic seller in all of us.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;THE SKILL SET:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Bachelor’s degree in Accounting&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;5+ years of progressive corporate accounting experience&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Comfortable working on a fast-paced team with changing priorities within a high-growth company&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong communication, interpersonal, and presentation skills to interact with various levels of management and build influential relationships with partners in the business&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Positive attitude with a high level of eagerness and aptitude to learn new technology and practices&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Demonstrated ability to multi-task and balance numerous priorities in a fast-paced operational environment.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong knowledge of Excel, with experience in NetSuite a plus&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Hands-on experience processing US multi-state payroll&lt;/strong&gt;, including federal, state, and local tax filings (Forms 941, W-2, state equivalents)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Experience coordinating or processing international payroll&lt;/strong&gt; across multiple countries (e.g., UK, Mexico, Poland, India), including working with in-country payroll vendors or PEO providers&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Knowledge with US GAAP and international accounting principles&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Familiarity with payroll compliance requirements, including garnishments, equity compensation taxation, and expatriate/shadow payroll concepts is a plus&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;At Clari + Salesloft, we are committed to creating an inclusive and supportive workplace where everyone belongs and can thrive. We focus on culture add, not culture fit, and believe our teams are made stronger by the unique perspectives, experiences, and identities each person brings.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We are proud to be an Equal Opportunity Employer and provide employment opportunities to all employees and applicants without regard to race, color, religion, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, national origin, age, disability, veteran status, pregnancy, or any other characteristic protected by law.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;If you’re excited about this role even though your experience may not perfectly match every requirement, we encourage you to apply. We are actively hiring across multiple geographies and would love to welcome passionate, curious, and mission-driven individuals to our growing team. Explore our open roles and consider joining us!&lt;/p&gt;
